  "summary": "Software Engineering\n- Received 2nd place at 2020 ACM Mid-Southeast Conference for Autonomous Flight Monitoring and Control Software.\n- Summer research with professor on the setup and use of a Hadoop distributed cluster.\n- Created a Map-Reduce program to analyze public GitHub repos and determine which programmers are the most profane in their code.\n- Ported popular mobile game Flappy Bird to C# WPF Application. \n\nAerospace and Robotics\n- Team member of the UTM Aero Design Team from 2019-2021 as Software Design Lead.\n- Designed and implemented flight control and autopilot software for competition aircraft entered into The SAE Aero Design Competition.\n- Modified Micropython port of ESP32 firmware to support longer range WIFI requirements needed to facilitate high data rate wireless telemetry and control of aircraft.\n\nSkills and Interests\n- Greatly interested in developing software to interact closely with hardware sensors. (Navigation and environmental awareness of software especially.)\n- Passionate about teaching and leadership development\n- Languages: Proficient in C++, Java, C#, Python, JavaScript, HTML, and C; also familiar with Haskell, Prolog, and Clingo.\n- Tools:  CLion, IntelliJ, PyCharm, Visual Studio, VS Code, LaTeX, Git, GitHub.\n\nMy email is andltayl(at)ut.utm.edu if you'd like to chat!",
